      "message": "The parse_var_ref below finds it var const we are referencing the variable in another hist trigger and creates a var_ref field.\n\ne.g.\necho \u0027hist:keys\u003dcommon_pid:granularity\u003d0x80000\u0027 \u003e\u003e events/kmem/rss_stat\necho \u0027hist:keys\u003dcommon_pid:vals\u003d$granularity\u0027 \u003e\u003e events/kmem/rss_stat\n\nWe use this for the case when referencing a var const that is local to the hist trigger currently being defined and so as to not create an addition var_ref field.",
